463 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (India was a diverse country with a multitude of local customs, traditions, and legal systems prior to British colonial rule. The Britishers recognized the need for a unified and comprehensive legal code that could replace the existing complex and often conflicting legal systems. The Criminal Law reflected the interests and priorities of the British colonial administration. It included provisions that were beneficial to colonial rulers and served their interests in maintaining law and order. Overall, the enactment of the criminal laws served both administrative and control purposes for the British colonial government in India. It provided a legal framework that was conducive to British governance and the maintenance of order in a diverse and complex colonial society. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
464 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (In the field of law, there are two fundamental categories that are often used to classify legal principles and rules: substantive law and procedural law. These two categories work together to create a comprehensive legal system. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
465 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Substantive law, sometimes referred to as "real law," encompasses the actual laws and regulations that govern people's behaviour and define their rights and obligations. It defines what is legal or illegal, and it outlines the rights and duties of individuals and entities. For example-  criminal law, contract law, property law, family law, and more. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
466 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Procedural law, on the other hand, governs the process by which legal cases are conducted. It outlines the rules, procedures, and methods that must be followed when pursuing a legal claim, defending against one, or resolving disputes.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
467 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (In the present newsletter we will be covering  The Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023 referred as Substantive Law & The  Bharatiya Sakshya Bill, 2023, The Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023 referred as Procedural law.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
