577 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Ensure that the legislation not only focuses on punishing offenders but also incorporates measures for safeguarding, compensating, and rehabilitating victims, especially in instances involving violence and exploitation. In the current BNS \(present bill\), we can observe specific sections, such as Clause 65, 70 & 122, that address these aspects comprehensively.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
578 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (CLARITY &  PRECISION :)
/E (CLARITY &  PRECISION :)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
579 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (It is crucial to guarantee that the language used in the BNS is unambiguous and exact, minimizing the potential for confusion. Ambiguous legal clauses can result in varying interpretations. In the current bill, there are instances where clarity is lacking, such as the absence of a definition for "Community Service" in the context of the sixth type of punishment .)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
580 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (In conclusion, it's important to recognize that there is always room for improvement in any legislative bill. When a bill is presented before a standing committee, there is the opportunity for thorough review, and the committee may propose changes and amendments to enhance its effectiveness and clarity. This process underscores the dynamic and responsive nature of the legislative system, aiming to ensure that the final law serves the best interests of society.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
