749 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Some provisions in the BNS have been criticised for upholding gender biases. For example, offences related to sexuality and marriage often favour a male-centric perspective . Right to privacy of men is also not taken into consideration under BNS, one of the biggest critiques of Bill. Like when we look at Clause 76 for Voyeurism & Clause 77 For Stalking, it is clearly evident that these sections don't talk anything about the privacy of male. No concerns are shown towards their privacy. It's purely covering & aiming towards engaging in private acts of Women. )
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
750 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (INADEQUATE VICTIM SUPPORT :)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
751 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The IPC focuses mainly on punishing the offender and could be more comprehensive in providing support for victims .There are only few clauses out of 356 clauses where victim compensation are seen i.e. u/c 65 Punishment for rape in certain cases , u/c 70 for Gang rape & u/c 122 for Voluntarily causing hurt or grievous hurt by use of acid, etc)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
752 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (AMBIGUITY: )
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
753 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The new bill does not explicitly mention whether criticism of the government, without inciting violence or illegal activities, constitutes an offence, it may create ambiguity or uncertainty in how such actions would be treated under section 150 of BNS. In many democratic societies, freedom of speech is protected as a fundamental right, and citizens have the right to express their opinions, including criticism of the government, as long as it does not incite violence or pose a direct threat to national security. Critics have raised concerns about the bill's lack of explicit instructions regarding the enforcement of specific provisions concerning sexual offences, particularly the one pertaining to false promises of marriage.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
