/K [12]
>>
endobj
1121 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The definition of 'corporation' in the BNSS requires an update to include newer definitions from legislation like the Companies Act, 2013. Critics have raised concerns regarding  Clause 262 of the BNSS, which permits an accused to apply for discharge within 60 days of the framing of charges, which appears to contradict established legal principles. )
/Pg 50 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
1122 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Clarity is essential in this context, and consideration of alternative triggers, such as the filing of a charge sheet or police report, may be necessary. Additionally, Clause 250 of the BNSS needs better clarification concerning discharge before formal charges are framed.)
/Pg 50 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
